<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abd al-Aziz al-Fishtali</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1549–1621</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abd <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-aziz">al-Aziz</a> al-Fishtali was a Moroccan scholar, poet and court historian of the Saadi sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-al-mansur">Ahmad al-Mansur</a>, in whose chancery he served as a leading secretary. His chronicle Manahil al-Safa celebrated al-Mansur's reign, including the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai</a> in 1591, and is a principal source for Saadi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>.</p></div>
